BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[B] Walk and Words: A Hike and Workshop With Belmont's Poet Laurea
 te
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260720T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260720T193000
DTSTAMP:20260703T225103Z
UID:smcl-6a3eecb47e16a03d00e854d6@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Belmont's Poet Laureate\, Greg McCulloh\, for a unique o
 utdoor experience that combines a scenic hike at Waterdog Lake with a poet
 ry workshop. Participants will draw inspiration from nature\, engage in gu
 ided writing exercises\, and explore the connection between movement\, obs
 ervation\, and storytelling. Whether you're an experienced writer or simpl
 y curious about poetry and creative expression\, all are welcome. Come enj
 oy the outdoors\, connect with fellow community members\, and discover new
  ways to find words in the world around you. Please note we will be starti
 ng at the Belmont library. Please wear comfortable clothing and bring a wa
 ter bottle to stay hydrated. Notebooks and pens will be provided. This eve
 nt is open to teens and adults. Registration is required. Please check in
  for this event in that Taube Room!\n\nAges: 12-18\nRegistration: require
 d\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a3eecb47e16a03d00e854d6\
 nLast synced: 2026-07-03 15:51 PDT
LOCATION:Belmont
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a3eecb47e16a03d00e854d6
END:VEVENT
