BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[B] Paws for Tales
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260721T183000
DTSTAMP:20260703T225103Z
UID:smcl-6a4591f9a03157457d04f4ce@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Do you have an enthusiastic reader? Or perhaps a bit more relu
 ctant one\, by chance? If so\, consider signing your child up for the fun 
 experience of reading to a therapy dog at our library!\n\nStudies show tha
 t children who may feel reluctant to read in front of their peers are much
  less anxious when an animal is present\, as they don't perceive them as j
 udgmental. So\, reading aloud to them often helps children become much mor
 e comfortable with their reading.\n\nAnd with this highly experienced grou
 p of therapy dogs at Belmont...even children who are not yet reading thems
 elves can still join in\, as families are welcome to sit down together to 
 share a book and entertain these pups with a bedtime story.\n\nWe also hav
 e on tap each time a seasonal crafting activity for all ages & generations
  to take part in & connect over!\nIt's a sweet way to pass the minutes\, w
 hile awaiting your child's scheduled time\, with one of these incredibly t
 rained dogs.\n\nDoes this sound like a fun evening for your family? Then d
 on't forget to sign up for your own 10-minute slot at smcl.org/pawsfortale
 s.\n\nSigning up ahead of time also helps us best plan for the number of d
 ogs to have on hand. Hope you can join us!\n\n(Our sincerest thanks go to 
 the amazing Pet Assisted Therapy teams\, who make this program possible - 
 certified by the Peninsula Humane Society & SPCA's Paws for Tales program)
 \n\nAges: 6-11\nRegistration: none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com
 /events/6a4591f9a03157457d04f4ce\nLast synced: 2026-07-03 15:51 PDT
LOCATION:Belmont
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a4591f9a03157457d04f4ce
END:VEVENT
